{"agent":"phview-lane","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`phase_status` computes `ready` and `blocked` with the requested agent (`agent=agent or log.agent_id`), but `_next_blocking_dep` calls `plan(st, cfg, kind=\"task\", phase=phase_id, with_deps=True)` without passing any agent. When a caller requests a non-default agent, e.g. `phase_status(repo, \"p\", agent=\"alice\")`, the row’s `ready`/`blocked` fields can be agent-scoped while `next_blocking_dep` is computed under the default agent scope. That can return a `next_blocking_dep` that is ready for the default agent but not for the requested agent, so the fields in the same row describe different agents.","digest":"e0c9c6263cacba06","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/api/viewers.py:_next_blocking_dep","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/viewers.py:_next_blocking_dep"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"When `tasks` is truthy, `_list_read` calls `_api().view_read(repo, \"task\", phase=..., limit=..., offset=..., all=...)` and drops every other filter that `ddflow_list` documents. For example, a tool call `{\"kind\":\"phase\",\"tasks\":\"P1\",\"state\":\"open\",\"tag\":\"wave:2\"}` will return tasks from phase `P1` regardless of their state or tag, because `state`, `tag`, `owner`, `query`, `since`, `item`, `match`, `mode`, `sources`, and `source` are never forwarded to `view_read`; completed tasks or tasks with other wave tags appear even though the caller explicitly asked for only open `wave:2` tasks. The tool schema exposes those properties, so silently ignoring them is wrong.","digest":"c2e8252eff7a449b","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:_list_read","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:_list_read"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":19608,"diff_sha":"d8b2ddb203a3c128729224ba7c8140607362f474bf51f5e173b53f779f41b173","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/PH-phase-view","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":376.4,"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"a7289322a15b5f29","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/PH-phase-view.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T070646Z-dbfbe21e.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewed_head":"2a1d55e741ae2e1c73d82bb19c742a48a660faf1","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/viewers.py":"100644 809c58a742b4a9bce7dfadb57a1b330f57c205d9","ddflow/services/viewers.py":"100644 815a53a7fdd5260a22d2d7f151a219ac14811638","ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py":"100644 278d987180fa6013bf60b7053bdfffa2591a6dd3","ddflow/surfaces/tools/families.py":"100644 565a0e38187b98858a1ccefee9b81cf508102a40","ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py":"100644 5745439bcd75302c59e7693e32bfa8e4dd94d2ec","tests/test_phase_view.py":"100644 fb2b0dd37450927c19ffec68a332efd6d750e825"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/viewers.py:_next_blocking_dep","ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:_list_read"],"tree_sha":"2a1d55e741ae+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":2},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"eca4025c13986064d0fe3f7f0","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":191354,"schema":1,"subject":"PH-phase-view","ts":"2026-11-13T07:13:03.334941Z"}
{"agent":"phview-lane","data":{"gate":"critic"},"id":"eb2a658ab94b4d03484aff1dc","kind":"gate.started","lamport":191355,"schema":1,"subject":"PH-phase-view","ts":"2026-11-13T07:13:05.861033Z"}
{"agent":"phview-lane","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"The `phase list --tasks` expansion prints only the task row's own `needs` (`needs = r.get(\"needs\") or []`), but the project guidance states that a task inherits the needs of its phase and that phase needs must be read before placing a task [r-task-phase-needs-wave]. Given a phase `P` with `needs: [\"Q\"]` and a task `T` in `P` with no explicit `needs`, `ddflow phase list --tasks P` prints `T` with no `needs` annotation, making it appear unblocked even though its effective dependency set includes `Q` through the phase. The view therefore presents an incomplete dependency list.","digest":"2abb82a4309a41a4","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py:_print_phase_tasks","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py:_print_phase_tasks"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"`_list_read` treats any truthy `tasks` value as a request for the phase’s task list and unconditionally calls `view_read(repo, \"task\", phase=...)`, ignoring the caller’s `kind` and other list parameters. The property description says `tasks` is meaningful when `kind=phase`, but a valid call such as `{\"kind\": \"decision\", \"tasks\": \"phase-1\", \"query\": \"foo\"}` returns the task list for `phase-1` instead of decisions matching `foo`; similarly `{\"kind\": \"task\", \"tasks\": \"phase-1\", \"state\": \"done\"}` ignores `state` and returns the default phase task view. This silently returns the wrong rows for the requested kind/filter.","digest":"aa1e1895e5ab1e51","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:_list_read","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:_list_read"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The new `_task` helper creates tasks with only `--phase`, `--title`, and `--globs`, and the direct `task add` call in `test_phase_list_tasks_expands_one_phase_inline_needs` also omits any wave tag. This violates the recorded project rule [r-task-phase-needs-wave], which requires every task to carry a `wave:N` tag and to explicitly state its dependency state, including `no-deps` for tasks with no prerequisites. For example, `test_phase_list_annotates_every_phase_row_with_ready` adds `P1.T1` and `P1.T2` without wave/no-deps information, so the test is asserting READY behavior on tasks that do not satisfy the project's required task shape; if the READY/tally logic is wave-aware or validates task shape, this test data is invalid and the assertion can be wrong.","digest":"84d0dc4df5f133a5","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_phase_view.py:_task","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_phase_view.py:_task"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":19608,"diff_sha":"d8b2ddb203a3c128729224ba7c8140607362f474bf51f5e173b53f779f41b173","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/PH-phase-view","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":434.0,"family":"alibaba","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"122930c8de5ba5e9","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/PH-phase-view.critic.[REDACTED:name].20261113T071305Z-7073eafe.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewed_head":"2a1d55e741ae2e1c73d82bb19c742a48a660faf1","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/viewers.py":"100644 809c58a742b4a9bce7dfadb57a1b330f57c205d9","ddflow/services/viewers.py":"100644 815a53a7fdd5260a22d2d7f151a219ac14811638","ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py":"100644 278d987180fa6013bf60b7053bdfffa2591a6dd3","ddflow/surfaces/tools/families.py":"100644 565a0e38187b98858a1ccefee9b81cf508102a40","ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py":"100644 5745439bcd75302c59e7693e32bfa8e4dd94d2ec","tests/test_phas