{"agent":"phview-lane","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"The new `--tasks` expansion returns before `_query(a, kind)` is ever called, so list filters accepted by `phase list` are silently discarded. For example, with the generic `--query` filter used by the normal list path, `ddflow phase list --tasks P --query fix` takes the new early return, calls `_print_phase_tasks`, which runs `view_list(c.repo, \"task\", phase=a.tasks)` without the query, and prints every task in phase `P` even though the caller asked to restrict the output to tasks matching `fix`. The accepted filter is ignored, so the command reports a wrong task set and exits OK.","digest":"f1dce7618e122340","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py:cmd_list","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py:cmd_list"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"When `tasks` is supplied with `kind=phase`, the new `_list_read` path calls `view_read` with only `phase`, `limit`, `offset`, and `all`, dropping the other documented list filters. For example, `{\"kind\": \"phase\", \"tasks\": \"P1\", \"state\": \"done\"}` returns every task in `P1`, including open/blocked tasks, because `state` is not forwarded; the same applies to `query`, `tag`, `owner`, etc. The kind guard fixes the wrong-kind case, but the prior finding’s “other list parameters ignored” problem still holds for the allowed `kind=phase`: an agent asking for a filtered task list receives an unfiltered list and may treat undone/non-matching tasks as satisfying the filter.","digest":"7537799db30c6de9","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:_list_read","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:_list_read"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":20200,"diff_sha":"60689959304be16c0523