{"agent":"phview-lane","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":5,"detail":"The tasks expansion still drops the documented `query` list filter. A tool call such as `{\"kind\":\"phase\",\"tasks\":\"P1\",\"query\":\"login\"}` is accepted, but `_list_read` builds `common` without `query` and returns `_api().view_read(repo, \"task\", phase=\"P1\", **common)`, so every task in phase `P1` is returned rather than only tasks matching `login`. The non-tasks branch passes `query=_arg(a, \"query\")` to `view_read`, so task lists do support query filtering; omitting it here silently produces an over-broad result and contradicts the stated “same list filters” behavior.","digest":"129cd68583844153","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:_list_read","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:_list_read"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The new tests do not exercise the round-2 filter pass-through behavior. The only `--tasks` test calls `phase list --tasks P1 --json` with no other list filters. If the implementation regresses to the previously confirmed pattern (`view_list(c.repo, \"task\", phase=a.tasks)` without forwarding `state`, `tag`, `owner`, `query`, `since`, `limit`, etc.), this test still passes because no filters are supplied, so the claimed fix is unguarded by the new test suite.","digest":"fc55207a9ff28b99","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_phase_view.py:test_phase_list_tasks_expands_one_phase_inline_needs","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_phase_view.py:test_phase_list_tasks_expands_one_phase_inline_needs"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":20379,"diff_sha":"9d15fa186dfd7d93cac812668e56a62c0825780926b4aa7dd899cbb556481f56","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/PH-phase-view","diff_stat":{