{"agent":"phview-lane","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":5,"detail":"The new `tasks` expansion still drops the `query` filter. `ddflow_list` accepts `query`, and the non-`tasks` path forwards it via `query=_arg(a, \"query\")`, but when `a[\"tasks\"]` is truthy and `kind == \"phase\"` the function builds `common` without `query` and returns `_api().view_read(repo, \"task\", phase=_arg(a, \"tasks\"), **common)`. Thus a tool call like `{\"kind\": \"phase\", \"tasks\": \"P1\", \"query\": \"fix\"}` returns every task in phase `P1` instead of only tasks matching `fix`; the equivalent filtered list call `{\"kind\": \"task\", \"phase\": \"P1\", \"query\": \"fix\"}` would filter. This is the remaining part of the prior filter-through finding: `state`, `tag`, `owner`, `since`, `item`, and `match` are now passed through, but `query` is not.","digest":"95c7bdcaf6a14371","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:_list_read","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:_list_read"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":21413,"diff_sha":"290704661bd9d15f946ddce9312d0c6a845ea5658119d93d5cfafee4475dce49","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/PH-phase-view","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1.9,"family":"alibaba","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"7224f53f7d6f88fa","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/PH-phase-view.critic.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261113T080106Z-ebe09bda.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"606085c4959f8f4e75496bc8a0d612236b6acf94","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/viewers.py":"100644 9206573ee3b8d84731556d7b51daead422292d01","ddflow/services/viewers.py":"100644 d810f1c0e0ba7155fa2c746c3fff2b00ff6c9884","ddflow/su